WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.760
Seesen, Germany, 1810.

2
00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:04.990
A new Jewish temple opens.

3
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:08.270
An organ plays, and the
sermon is in German.

4
00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.470
In 1818, the Hamburg Temple follows.

5
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.540
Its prayer book alters old
prayers for a return to Zion.

6
00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:20.100
Reformers wanted a Judaism that
modern Jews would not leave behind.

7
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:23.760
So can a religion change
its prayers and its laws,

8
00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:25.850
and still be the same religion?

9
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:30.090
In this mission, you'll find out why
the first Reformers made these changes,

10
00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:33.210
and how Orthodox Jews
see the Torah instead.

11
00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:37.940
Then you'll build an argument map, and
weigh up a claim about Reform for yourself.

12
00:00:37.990 --> 00:00:42.690
Your mission: weigh up whether a religion
can change its prayers and its laws

13
00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.510
and still be the same religion.
